# Feature 2274, 2026-10-30. The debugger's formatter shows a map of more than
# `SORTED` entries (1,024) in the order its keys were first written, read from
# the order region the runtime keeps after the values, and says so; until then
# it showed the buckets' order, the hash's. Its children follow the same order.
# A thousand and one hundred keys, `i * 7919 % 1100`, are written in an order
# neither sorted nor the hash's, so an order kept by accident cannot pass.

function main()
    m: {i64: i64} @= {}
    i @= 0

    while i < 1100
        m[i * 7919 % 1100] @ i
        i @ i + 1

    print(m.len())
